# AM01 Mining Daemon Configuration
#
# Read by odo-miner.service. Apply changes with:
#   systemctl restart odo-miner
#
# Only DAEMON_OPTS is passed to the daemon. The user, working directory and
# binary path are set literally in the unit file -- systemd cannot take those
# from environment variables, so setting them here would have no effect.
#
# The binary is /usr/bin/odo-miner and it runs as the 'miner' user from
# /var/lib/odo-miner.

# Daemon options: stratum server, worker, optional password
#   --host POOL_HOST --port POOL_PORT --worker WALLET.WORKER [--pass PASSWORD]
#
# Set your pool and wallet here before starting the miner. The value below is
# a placeholder and will not connect to anything.
# POSITIONAL: <host> <port> <worker> [password]. There is no option parser.
#
# This file used to read
#   DAEMON_OPTS="--host test-pool.example.com --port 3333 --worker ..."
# and odo-miner's main() takes argv[1..4] positionally -- so a user editing it
# per its own instructions got "--host" resolved as the hostname and their
# pool name resolved as the port. The daemon then failed, Restart=on-failure
# with StartLimitIntervalSec=0 retried for ever, and the journal reported a
# DNS error naming a string the user never typed.
#
# post-image.sh and am01-panel-helper both already wrote it correctly; this
# file, the one a user actually finds on the running board, did not.
DAEMON_OPTS="test-pool.example.com 3333 YOUR_WALLET.am01 x"

# Leave DAEMON_OPTS empty to bring the daemon up without mining, which is
# useful when bringing up the FPGA bus for the first time:
#   DAEMON_OPTS=""

# Optional: DS18B20 temperature sensor for fan control. Empty = not connected.
TEMP_SENSOR_ID=

# Optional: GPIO pin for fan PWM control (BCM GPIO number). Empty = disabled.
FAN_PWM_GPIO=

# Logging level (if supported by build)
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
